WEBVTT

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:00.930
Welcome back.

00:00:01.170 --> 00:00:06.130
Well, here we are on the last show of the ninth television series, and I'm certainly glad

00:00:06.130 --> 00:00:06.950
you joined me today.

00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:11.840
So for this show, I thought we'd do something a little bit different, a nice, happy little

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:12.200
painting.

00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:17.920
And I've already started out here, and I've taken liquid black, as you can see, and went

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:21.680
right around here, and then right in the center, just liquid white, and sort of let them blend

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:23.620
together right here where they come together.

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:28.860
Liquid black is exceptionally good for areas where you're going to have a lot of dark shadows,

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:29.760
very dark colors.

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:29.920
using.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:31.420
put that in, saves you a lot of work.

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:34.020
So let's have them graphically run all the colors

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:35.800
across the screen that you need

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:37.460
to paint this painting along with me,

00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:39.110
and we'll come on up here and get started.

00:00:40.170 --> 00:00:44.190
Alrighty, let's start off today with a touch of phthalo blue.

00:00:44.490 --> 00:00:46.250
And we'll just tap a little of that into the brush,

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:49.200
and we can add a little black to that too,

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:50.100
just to dull it down.

00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:53.600
There we go, small amount of color.

00:00:54.230 --> 00:00:54.990
Let's go right up here.

00:00:55.660 --> 00:00:58.040
Start right at the top, and as usual,

00:00:58.310 --> 00:00:59.840
make our little criss-cross.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:06.840
just like so, just like so, very nice, easy to do.

00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:15.490
And we'll bring it down to about like that, okay.

00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:18.770
And very gently go across to take out the brush strokes.

00:01:19.870 --> 00:01:21.750
And that quick, we got a happy little sky.

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:25.990
We'll wash our brush, shake off the excess,

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:29.980
and we'll get to it.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:33.090
the camera man again, he has caught the devil.

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:36.380
I'm gonna go right into titanium white

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:38.300
and just pull that brush through it,

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:40.120
just tap a little color right into it.

00:01:41.140 --> 00:01:42.040
Okay, let's go right up here.

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:43.800
Maybe there's a happy little cloud

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:45.020
that lives up here in the sky.

00:01:45.450 --> 00:01:47.800
It just sort of floats around, see?

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:51.000
Just sort of pull it around like that.

00:01:51.530 --> 00:01:53.370
This is just straight titanium white

00:01:53.370 --> 00:01:54.960
and we just want the indication

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:56.440
of a little something happening in there.

00:01:56.480 --> 00:01:57.860
We're not looking for a lot of detail.

00:01:59.600 --> 00:01:59.960
Far away.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:08.780
There we are, and that quick, we have a happy little cloud.

00:02:09.890 --> 00:02:11.990
In this series, we've made a lot of different clouds.

00:02:12.230 --> 00:02:14.670
We've made some great big stormy clouds,

00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:17.260
and some with a lot of color in them.

00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:21.920
And we've made some beautiful seascapes.

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:25.020
I really, really hope you've enjoyed those also.

00:02:26.010 --> 00:02:27.590
Let's build us a little mountain back here.

00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:28.700
Let's take some black.

00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:33.460
Got some Van Dyke brown, a little touch of blue.

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:35.960
Shoot, let's throw some crimson in there too.

00:02:36.910 --> 00:02:39.670
So we got blue, brown, Lizarin crimson, and black.

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:42.030
Pull it out very flat.

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:45.910
Now, cut across and get our little roll of paint.

00:02:46.030 --> 00:02:48.040
We always use that little roll of paint, okay?

00:02:48.810 --> 00:02:51.900
Now then, we're gonna have a nice little mountain

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:53.140
that lives way back here.

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:55.540
Push that paint right into the fabric.

00:02:56.980 --> 00:02:59.980
Just really push hard, work it in.

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:08.340
Just push it, there we go, there he is.

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:10.100
The only thing you're worried about

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:11.620
is this nice outside edge.

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:19.750
Okay, we'll take a large brush, grab it, and pull.

00:03:19.930 --> 00:03:29.760
Let it blend with the liquid white, and it just disappears.

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:32.890
right into nothing, just a nice misty effect.

00:03:34.920 --> 00:03:39.080
Okay, let's take a little titanium white,

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:43.080
cut us off a small little roll of paint, just a tiny bit.

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:48.790
And let's go up here and just let the knife float.

00:03:49.940 --> 00:03:50.980
Just let it float.

00:03:52.070 --> 00:03:55.160
We'll put in some nice highlights.

00:03:56.900 --> 00:03:58.260
And you could do this in colors.

00:03:58.580 --> 00:03:59.980
You might wanna, you might.

00:04:00.410 --> 00:04:03.470
that's brown with all kinds of beautiful rocks and stones.

00:04:04.170 --> 00:04:07.600
Works the same way, same way.

00:04:09.150 --> 00:04:10.770
So in your world, you decide,

00:04:11.460 --> 00:04:13.620
and you make it any way that you want it.

00:04:14.860 --> 00:04:17.740
Let's take some white, some phthalo blue,

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:21.860
add a little bit of Van Dyke brown to that.

00:04:22.270 --> 00:04:22.890
There we go.

00:04:23.500 --> 00:04:26.140
The brown is just used to dull that blue down a little bit

00:04:26.140 --> 00:04:27.380
so it's not quite so bright.

00:04:28.460 --> 00:04:29.640
Cut off that little roll of paint.

00:04:30.640 --> 00:04:33.770
Okay, now then, come right back in here.

00:04:35.310 --> 00:04:37.240
See there, that easy, easy.

00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:39.850
Just put in some nice little shadows.

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:45.580
Just sort of let those work right together, together.

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:49.720
Then you can wander back in here

00:04:49.720 --> 00:04:51.410
and pick up some of the whites.

00:04:52.290 --> 00:04:54.050
Boy, you can just make all kinds of things

00:04:54.050 --> 00:04:57.300
happen in your mountain, all kinds.

00:04:57.480 --> 00:04:59.320
You're limited only by your imagination.

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:04.050
Only by that, nothing else.

00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:09.080
But you can see in your mind, you can put on canvas.

00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:12.740
Here we are.

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:17.640
An artist, maybe imagination is one of the most important things

00:05:17.640 --> 00:05:19.240
that you can possess.

00:05:20.600 --> 00:05:22.410
So, develop your imagination.

00:05:24.160 --> 00:05:25.780
It's like any other muscle in the body.

00:05:25.960 --> 00:05:29.400
Use it, use it, exercise it, practice with it.

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:32.500
You'll be amazed at what you can imagine.

00:05:34.340 --> 00:05:39.040
Pretty soon, if you paint, you become very aware of nature.

00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:41.000
You become aware of color.

00:05:42.140 --> 00:05:43.680
